1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,191
The pegs have become posts, and the posts have become a camp. People call it Rim, because it sits on the lip of a door and pretends to be a border.

2
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:11,064
There is laundry, a radio, and a bell no one agreed to hang. Children from the camp learn the hours by the chord under their feet.

3
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:13,191
Once a week Sera carries a slate up the stair. Surface children and house children sit on the same step. She teaches them the guest law before she teaches them sums.

4
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:13,191
Minister Adler files a mineral claim on water that has not left the mountain. The form has a box for owner. He writes the name of the Compact in the box.

5
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:13,617
Sera writes the guest law where everyone must pass. A guest may drink. A guest may not carry the well away. A guest who lifts a weapon turns, and goes back up.

6
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:12,766
Bread and oil move across the threshold in open baskets. For a while there is no price. Then a chalkboard appears in the camp, and the baskets start to hesitate.

7
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:11,064
Adler's office publishes a map on which the gardens have numbers. The fruit trees are marked as yield. The school step is not marked at all.

8
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:14,043
The children turn the chord into a song and sing it wrong on purpose. The wrong notes do not change the timing. Every one hundred and eight seconds, the mountain agrees with itself.

9
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:12,766
Jun Park, who drives supplies along the rim, sits in the empty chair. He eats. He thanks the room. He comes back the next week, and the week after that.

10
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:11,489
By 2461 the chair has a cushion. No one has assigned it. Below, that is enough. Above, Adler adds the cushion to a list of unregulated hospitality.
